00:00.000 --> 00:10.289
Soon, you'll hand an AI agent your card and say: go buy what we need. It will say yes. The harder question is whether it could ever say no.

00:10.289 --> 00:27.384
Here's what we kept running into. People run on doctrine: the customer is always right, make it right. An agent doesn't have that instinct. It has rules, logic, and whatever it can measure. And it is between the doctrine and the statute that we spent our focus during the Meta Global AI Developer Hackathon.

00:27.384 --> 00:45.593
We watched Muse Spark work in the open, and we tried to measure what she does. But ask where any of it is written down. How is it measured? From a developer standpoint, it is an opaque mixture of trust and faith.

00:45.593 --> 01:03.281
Picture the errand. Go to the store, buy what we need. The listing says thirty-eight fifty. The register says forty-two fifty, and the agent pays it, because arguing isn't its job. The box shows up in black, with a phone case nobody ordered. And when you look for what happened, all you get is the agent's word for it.

01:03.281 --> 01:12.638
Now look at both sides of the counter. You ask for a return: sorry, try again later. The store asks for the extra charge and the extended warranty.

01:12.638 --> 01:22.541
That's backwards. Think about how you actually shop. Not that one, not that colour, too much, until one thing is left. A yes only means something from a system that can say no.

01:22.541 --> 01:36.700
Europe's AI Act wrote duties of disclosure, of records that must be kept and verifiable. Oversight that must be real. A statute can name the duties. Only an environment can perform them: claim, measurement, verdict, receipt, at the moment of the act.

01:36.700 --> 01:46.700
So we didn't build a better agent. We built the room around her. We call this room Runway. Muse Spark gets a mandate she can't edit, gates that re-check every claim, and a receipt that seals the reason either way.

01:47.433 --> 02:09.133
Tonight, someone will tell an AI assistant: reorder the usual. It will. And nobody — not you, not the store, not the law — will be able to check how. Getting an AI agent in service of legislation means buying exact. Every purchase is a string of claims: this is the item, this is the price, this is the seller. Every claim is measured on the Runway by a gating system, and if any come back wrong, the money doesn't move.

02:09.133 --> 02:27.733
The test is humble on purpose. A red gooseneck kettle, forty dollars. When the price drifts, she refuses and names why. When the seller has a history of drifting, the seller gets refused too. The delivery photo gets measured, not taken on faith: eighteen of twenty right, and we publish the two misses.

02:27.733 --> 02:39.433
That brings us back to legislative mandates. The receipt is the disclosure. The chain is the record. The named refusal is the oversight. Not by promising honesty. By measuring it.

02:39.433 --> 02:49.513
When an agent holds your savings, you don't want eagerness. You want the no, as many times as it takes, to reach the right yes.
